msgstr "[color=#696969][i]※Current location: Maze※[/i][/color]"

#: res://timelines/07_maze_entry.dtl:3
#. source-sha256: d9ba41000b6cce66b4f8e927068f443b49523972907958edacd9381da2f14b34
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_entry_001/text"
msgstr "The instant I step through the gate, an uncanny gust rises out of nowhere. I jump. Sand and dust whip into my eyes, and with a tremendous clang, the gate slams shut behind me."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_entry.dtl:5
#. source-sha256: 155abac40d30ace6deae3795e84432d6d8b8d8157b712c96a91240f2e7f88c92
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_entry_002/text"
msgstr "I stumble two steps forward. Several hands seem to catch me through the haze. Before I can look up, a voice at my ear says, “Careful, Your Highness! Don't fall!”"

#: res://timelines/07_maze_entry.dtl:7
#. source-sha256: 5ca6a7155636fd5b3cc645cafc0b1fc2e4c79cac8dd18e3fd36e2dc89facc705
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_entry_003/text"
msgstr "Who are they calling Your Highness? I focus on three unfamiliar faces, all watching me anxiously. One straightens my hem, another smooths the hair beside my ear, and the third holds my arm, reluctant to let go."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_entry.dtl:9
#. source-sha256: a6069f5c8b5efa7ddddc7ca28992c86202b38be335dd211a959f6a19fa56e7a8
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_entry_004/text"
msgstr "“Where am I? And who are you?” The three pause and exchange glances. The oldest replies, “Your Highness, this is Dew Garden. There's a performance today. Won't you join us?” He points farther inside. Sure enough, lights blaze there, and the faint clinking of cups reaches my ears."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_entry.dtl:11
#. source-sha256: 8676ada389c60338910f8fd92f45d43de691ab8d875da32592c6cbdeace083f4
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_entry_005/text"
msgstr "Something stirs in my chest. A delicious itch."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_entry.dtl:13
#. source-sha256: a2dc5853654bf735e5f10dafcd48bbb8611fe8f58c508c0868bafada828b3852
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_entry_006/text"
msgstr "—————— This is the place I've always longed for."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_entry.dtl:15
#. source-sha256: 5ac564e2fa20e321b5249471f8dbaf5d3cf211a703333c8eae8d897ab5e508fb
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_entry_007/text"
msgstr "I want to ask more, but the three slip away, bowing as they hurry off."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_entry.dtl:17
#. source-sha256: 64d0f17d989ac12086b668e3a2b59a98722be333673c59dab2d57a5b30dcd75c
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_entry_008/text"
msgstr "That's life. One moment I'm an ordinary citizen; the next, I'm {player_name}, revered by thousands! Frankly, this position suits my bearing much better."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_entry.dtl:19
#. source-sha256: 1288000b8f797a8e08be85e371d902f8894b5cfe7cf725040ac9c1735feaa7e0
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_entry_009/text"
msgstr "I'm the ruler here now. I want flowers by the armful, and money by the heap! Who would dare refuse me? Chest out, I swagger into the garden."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_entry.dtl:21
#. source-sha256: 786184d2ce86a751018cdd6950e7ce9e5c1adf1b051ac6b0e781990ece03c709
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_entry_010/text"
msgstr "But I can't get my bearings. I should:"

#: res://timelines/07_maze_exit.dtl:1
#. source-sha256: bffe4f4f56a40a7c5b9c32d8dbb4ce5b0d8ec81d7de0ae37c06b7ea556dfbb09
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_exit_000/text"
msgstr "[color=#696969][i]※Current location: Maze※[/i][/color]"

#: res://timelines/07_maze_exit.dtl:3
#. source-sha256: d54026ab80a0415657fb867fedd3c54acdbbbdd9cd76bd83b2277c4e612c12ec
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_exit_001/text"
msgstr "Wind pours in from the alley. White glue still marks the split at the toe of his leather shoe. The protagonist stands by the road, a few flowers weighing heavily against his chest. The purple-gray daylight seems filtered through old glass."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_exit.dtl:4
#. source-sha256: 985c83f3ec791c5af4a06d507fb4ef8838bbb1f9ba4d7527c31647d6c7dbe2db
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_exit_002/text"
msgstr "He looks down at himself and admits that this journey has already crushed his dreams of being a prince. But someone is still waiting up ahead. Whatever happens, he has to reach her."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_exit.dtl:7
#. source-sha256: 1027af3c9566525170e8f1fc03cf1a9bf1904a68b8e40861da3e989ddfb6f851
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_exit_004/text"
msgstr "Clutching the front of his coat, the protagonist follows the gray road toward the inpatient building."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_left.dtl:1
#. source-sha256: bffe4f4f56a40a7c5b9c32d8dbb4ce5b0d8ec81d7de0ae37c06b7ea556dfbb09
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_left_000/text"
msgstr "[color=#696969][i]※Current location: Maze※[/i][/color]"

#: res://timelines/07_maze_left.dtl:3
#. source-sha256: c98d754c3205accacbefe942af37bcbc3a10433c69b81e5779d6ecc731c4d8b7
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_left_001/text"
msgstr "The path leads through an archway into a garden. There is supposed to be a performance, but no stage; he wants flowers, but the lush plants bear none. A man in purple robes calls, “Well now, His Highness is here!” He clamps onto the protagonist's left arm and drags him into the crowd. When the protagonist tries to pull free, the grip tightens. The man whispers, “Your Highness, that woman from last month—her husband has been killed. Heh heh. She's being brought to you as we speak.”"

#: res://timelines/07_maze_left.dtl:6
#. source-sha256: 56bfdfe7a428c0bc44ad0fa2fcd60f9756b8a554e181aedc24bbc9d191177cde
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_left_003/text"
msgstr "He freezes for a second, then grins, showing rows of perfect teeth, his eyes glinting gold. He claps the protagonist hard on the back. “Your Highness! This wasn't my killing. You were the one who wanted him dead!”"

#: res://timelines/07_maze_left.dtl:7
#. source-sha256: 31eaaa78040e67f75d6edf7117e10042b86880d5d19b3f506a59668beb6e5442
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_left_004/text"
msgstr "The protagonist senses danger and wants to flee. His trapped hand has gone numb; no blood can get through. His left hand must be done for."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_left.dtl:8
#. source-sha256: 7e15773f92db02c1b5529f6891dbfd92a8f0f8fd68dae885b7b94401501fb6b7
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_left_005/text"
msgstr "Seeing his blank stare, the man asks, “Are you unwell, Your Highness? Where has your enthusiasm gone today?” He hauls the protagonist to the rockery maze entrance. “Go on in, Your Highness. Everything is ready.”"

#: res://timelines/07_maze_left.dtl:12
#. source-sha256: e98e90004e351893981d518195e479199fac98cabb7c83dbcda6e3aa159763c7
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_left_009/text"
msgstr "He mutters suspiciously, “Huh? You want the man too?” Then, “Very well, Your Highness. I'll have someone dig him up in a moment,” as he drags the protagonist to the rockery maze entrance."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_left.dtl:13
#. source-sha256: b47dcf553a4eedc59b8c7480985298fb7fe1ed1cd17d550a4cd1c90fc7a29901
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_left_010/text"
msgstr "“Go on in, Your Highness. Everything is ready.”"

#: res://timelines/07_maze_left.dtl:14
#. source-sha256: 88fe9ca3cb1c57cc4371b9039e6b625d0b7cf68291ade7d4c588585b772499e2
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_left_011/text"
msgstr "The protagonist asks what is ready, saying that this rockery maze would take two minutes to walk through. “You'll see when you get inside! Come now, don't keep us waiting.” With that, the man gives him a hard shove."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_middle.dtl:1
#. source-sha256: bffe4f4f56a40a7c5b9c32d8dbb4ce5b0d8ec81d7de0ae37c06b7ea556dfbb09
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_middle_000/text"
msgstr "[color=#696969][i]※Current location: Maze※[/i][/color]"

#: res://timelines/07_maze_middle.dtl:3
#. source-sha256: 1df2aa041a4fa34bd2f0074f0029be6dafc7e6e1d5f21e964489ceeec10d68e9
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_middle_001/text"
msgstr "The rockery passage grows narrower, the wind muffled between stone walls. Suddenly a fragrance reaches his nose, like a green orchid, so intense that it hardly seems of this world. Following the scent, the protagonist looks up and finds a green orchid blooming in a crack. He has never seen that color before. He can't resist picking it and slipping it into his sleeve pocket."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_middle.dtl:6
#. source-sha256: ed39e33eec28fde556cf9eee1d64bf20003316a81e34295f1b91756fc151727d
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_middle_003/text"
msgstr "Deeper in the rockery grows a clump of cacti, thick with spines. The protagonist reaches through them for a flower. The moment he snaps it off, a long, thin cut opens across his palm. Beads of blood seep out."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_middle.dtl:7
#. source-sha256: 755cd7541c6d0a2bf778449a165915c1c7c0152eab989f885a63ff846f00b509
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_middle_004/text"
msgstr "Looking at the wound, he suddenly thinks he may not be as powerful as he imagined. He hopes he isn't exceptional. Not at this moment, at least."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_middle.dtl:11
#. source-sha256: 698f89d9948c71225297dbe99d7ae1c84432732baba0dba8db85778103105ab2
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_middle_008/text"
msgstr "The green orchid is tucked into his sleeve, its fragrance still clinging to his fingers. The protagonist skirts the cacti and heads toward the center of the rockery."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_middle.dtl:15
#. source-sha256: 90a9a962c77d54a7512ca967f2d6927b9503abe358e0f325ccdf0ed660c39ab6
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_middle_012/text"
msgstr "He has the flower, but his palm won't stop tingling. Gripping the cactus flower, the protagonist walks on, turning that small cut over in his mind. The more he thinks, the hollower he feels."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_middle.dtl:19
#. source-sha256: 057b11434272531b304528111c519c9f5e13af3e900bfe6ad03c9523947c3ed8
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_middle_015/text"
msgstr "A woman stands at the center of the rockery, dressed in fine robes with a gold hairpin. Her features are beautiful enough, but she is too still to seem alive. A round blue hydrangea rests on her head. Her eyes are so clouded that the pupils are almost invisible; fine threads lift her eyelids, their ends sewn into her eyebrows. Her lips move slightly, her throat squeezing out an indistinct song. The words are unintelligible, as though she is singing to the air. Her arms hang limp, the backs of her hands covered in unreadable talismans. Her fingertips tremble."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_middle.dtl:20
#. source-sha256: f52265d36a7da268b29e84743a5fe2fbb676ffcdd1836dcf85bb090ed24845bc
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_middle_016/text"
msgstr "What is she? How is she standing?"

#: res://timelines/07_maze_middle.dtl:26
#. source-sha256: 91bf77636be3fbe9ee836f60a5a2eaf84884e40e9ae2c91deaa758097f305164
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_middle_021/text"
msgstr "He steps closer. A pole passes through the back of her clothing. Her sash is bound tightly around it, and the pole is driven into the ground, pinning her in the center of the rockery. Suddenly he understands what “Everything is ready” meant. This is a hell stripped of all humanity."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_middle.dtl:27
#. source-sha256: 6d4234d7fa24ea90df87df5c0548457f1a688c82df97f0b02a74def70a426616
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_middle_022/text"
msgstr "The world seems to spin, everything lurching sideways. He staggers backward, his throat tightening. “Animals. You're animals... I can't be a prince. I can't!”"

#: res://timelines/07_maze_middle.dtl:36
#. source-sha256: 1c7f12a13a97a042097540c8384761ae58f52b4a9ae66d90c685cec2ff18eb5a
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_middle_030/text"
msgstr "The protagonist forgets everything else and runs, bowling over anyone in his way as he bursts through the gate. A split opens at the toe of his leather shoe, the leather peeling back to reveal traces of white glue."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_middle.dtl:37
#. source-sha256: 202da085ae3f7f1df6a3a42fb4cf5c00a7372c7e4f8bccc17e7b1c4bf96ccf45
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_middle_031/text"
msgstr "He doesn't stop until the crossroads. Looking down, he counts the flowers in his arms and brushes dust off his clothes. When he looks up, the sun is purple-gray, as if something has veiled it."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_middle.dtl:41
#. source-sha256: c2c15ab4747815623a7773f0f10673a41c01a992bb649bfbef06ddc30f78a553
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_middle_034/text"
msgstr "The protagonist struggles to his feet, falls again, and finally braces his elbow against her shoulder to pull off the blue hydrangea. Her body is rigid, unlike a normal person's."

#: res://timelines/07_maze_middle.dtl:42
#. source-sha256: 19eb1724de20200dc703256650072198de3025d7447ff5d7b2e083c9f0bcae22
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_middle_035/text"
msgstr "Clutching the flower, he suddenly admits, “I don't have the courage to be a ruler. Cruelty and violence aren't my strengths. I'm just an ordinary person.”"

#: res://timelines/07_maze_right.dtl:1
#. source-sha256: bffe4f4f56a40a7c5b9c32d8dbb4ce5b0d8ec81d7de0ae37c06b7ea556dfbb09
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_right_000/text"
msgstr "[color=#696969][i]※Current location: Maze※[/i][/color]"

#: res://timelines/07_maze_right.dtl:3
#. source-sha256: 4f017c5f4ae38f582a2296e44d34c07c3a41796c49ef81aa797219c5c0fe875f
msgid "Text/lj_07_maze_right_001/text"
msgstr "I walk slowly along the winding path. Suddenly, voices drift over the wall. I tiptoe to a lattice window and peer through thick bamboo leaves at two people. One is dressed plainly. The other wears a black cloak, with a long gray-white beard and his hair in a topknot. Intricate patterns cover the cloak, like scorpions with human heads. Eavesdropping will probably take some effort (Energy -15)."

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:1
#. source-sha256: 7d00577939e19e4ae4f6816bc3e7d3134691b2d0752cd0a94edd40f3def1390c
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_000/text"
msgstr "[color=#696969][i]※Current location: My wife's hospital room※[/i][/color]"

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:4
#. source-sha256: 99c9c3b1ec20cd6ae3d95f2ae9fc315d00be25fb2589b0d35a2d4aa5b2c4ad9f
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_002/text"
msgstr "So much has happened today. I'm ready to tell my wife everything. Once she hears these stories, she'll understand how much I've done for her. I walk slowly toward her bed. The curtain is drawn. She and a nurse are talking behind it."

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:5
#. source-sha256: fb67d2d118e46841e2e8c77d68eade00f5b6f63d4c00f88534abc0ed82909a2c
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_003/text"
msgstr "“Is your husband coming today?”"

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:6
#. source-sha256: 5b905cfa390ac2efb84ba77bfc126791de089fca95ccb655b941309404a15f37
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_004/text"
msgstr "“I don't know. I don't care whether he comes.”"

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:7
#. source-sha256: 2ab941f594d4b14fce15c056f62b4593e9caa34242fb8a7bda2bf84b740c7638
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_005/text"
msgstr "“He brought nothing last time. I don't know who let him in.”"

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:8
#. source-sha256: c9a0ff99be7579b8c000a947844d432be6723ab57c9d937b17735b5ea62edd5c
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_006/text"
msgstr "“I'd rather he stayed away. Every time he comes, he acts like he's done something incredible. A simple hospital visit is an impossible feat for him.”"

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:9
#. source-sha256: 24b32f10e157dc0c8fd86a8bcc727a2a866e3c8ee8e30c337280e00945c31538
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_007/text"
msgstr "“He's your husband. The law says he has to come.”"

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:12
#. source-sha256: 33bac98d9144d9582eb7abd04bcc18daa60451174d959862556cae7664273497
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_009/text"
msgstr "I pull the curtain aside and meet the nurse's eyes. This time, I'm not empty-handed. I've brought {flower} flowers. “Your husband's here,” she tells my wife, then leaves."

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:13
#. source-sha256: 4f38a0de533a38519ae67d664cbe1fedbdd341f64ed21d4c9f9b778e880b6a89
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_010/text"
msgstr "My wife says nothing. She sits on the bed, facing the window, refusing to look at me."

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:14
#. source-sha256: 6f655e6a2e1b3141675f8a8a6897e40aa9f841fa5d1777d20d7994b6d4d03559
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_011/text"
msgstr "I put the flowers on her bedside cabinet and sit down nearby. Each of us waits for the other to speak. I'm desperate to tell her what happened in Dew Garden. My shoes are ruined; I ran into that neighbor I can't stand; and that damned idiot woman selling toadspawn—if it weren't for her, I'd have been here ages ago. I can't hold it in any longer."

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:15
#. source-sha256: 91db5941b7a09799c0bddbbc8a082fa55edc742084674173794db1f55627d559
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_012/text"
msgstr "“I wore out my shoes just getting here today.” She turns sharply. “Then don't come if your shoes are ruined!” Why is she suddenly so angry? I don't understand. I've worn these shoes for six or seven years. She's never offered to replace them. Now they're ruined, and she still couldn't care less."

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:16
#. source-sha256: 3ded6e1214e69d56036ea4459e40fd0fb5dff1f468260d52fc1a7262e8e97c8c
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_013/text"
msgstr "“I saw a living corpse in Dew Garden!” I lead with my most shocking encounter. Surely she'll want to know what happened. If she asks, I'll pour it all out, holding nothing back, beating my chest with every word."

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:17
#. source-sha256: f0b3c8a42e6d54498f256ad98af654062829cbe80a2de020581fa39a36113b93
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_014/text"
msgstr "“What time did you say you'd be here? And what time is it now? I've been waiting for you without even eating! If you're going to be late, at least call, so I can make other plans.” My wife ignores everything I've said. I feel angry and afraid at once. My mind goes blank. I don't know what I could possibly say to get her attention, to start telling her what's in my heart."

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:18
#. source-sha256: 46c613b5427f426bdf53dca7c9ab63813655491bee2e0b6c7ed5b05ccfb49881
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_015/text"
msgstr "“Did you feed the earthworm at home?” she asks. I can't answer at once. It escaped the day after she was admitted, and I haven't dared tell her. “Where's the earthworm?!” she demands angrily."

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:21
#. source-sha256: ffa1149c65ca594efb04f01b2b7ec52d72b5d7e3d8fe296ca5c3d6465b064acc
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_018/text"
msgstr "I take the earthworm out of my pocket. It isn't ours, but all earthworms look alike. She won't know the difference. Seeing that I can produce one, her expression softens a little."

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:24
#. source-sha256: 4b238f10d5854469fba5ac3b486659b9f7e42a0699a63206a091798a681a2bd1
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_020/text"
msgstr "“Have you no shame? Mixing fake flowers in with real ones. Nobody else is this shameless.”"

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:25
#. source-sha256: 969a75742c186e870b51f1f98b3182ba88fed18ba7ea71c943bdaa89b9c0e08e
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_021/text"
msgstr "“The flower shop owner stopped selling flowers,” I say desperately. “I searched the whole town. These were all I could find.”"

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:26
#. source-sha256: 3fbc19ad0905bb05d72fc1a8d41f64193a56382f3d706704aa49bcf32fe62e18
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_022/text"
msgstr "She snorts. “Then how did the person in the next bed manage to buy some?”"

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:27
#. source-sha256: 25987fdd82e5c74a449c1d4ffeb56467b386267ada294dd74089cfd3155bff2f
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_023/text"
msgstr "I'm speechless. How should I know how the person in the next bed got flowers?! That woman selling toadspawn really is targeting me. She must wait until I'm about to buy flowers, then switch to something else!"

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:29
#. source-sha256: 96c31a4097941b9ef1e170f37fbbfe6fde60bedf63b58689fc9d9e4c65cd3be9
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_026/text"
msgstr "“You just picked these up outside, didn't you? Too cheap to buy any?”"

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:30
#. source-sha256: 969a75742c186e870b51f1f98b3182ba88fed18ba7ea71c943bdaa89b9c0e08e
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_027/text"
msgstr "“The flower shop owner stopped selling flowers,” I say desperately. “I searched the whole town. These were all I could find.”"

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:31
#. source-sha256: 43d9a8f8fc6b949c5fb1cc522bd766a7eb776333439fb931ff4dc20ff941d35a
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_028/text"
msgstr "She gives a cold snort. Clearly, she doesn't believe me."

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:33
#. source-sha256: 94b2a90e5903726a6f53e0c17b628cdb48b125f48045d32ca867c08ecc3e3f83
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_032/text"
msgstr "“I'm so disappointed in you! We have no money as it is, and you don't lift a finger! Get out! I don't want to see you!”"

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:35
#. source-sha256: fb78bbb3002460a20f451d474b1110b5df0e10d4768278ac0d97eb82dfaefab2
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_034/text"
msgstr "“When can you leave the hospital?” It's the last thing I ask her."

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:36
#. source-sha256: e13533ff8159456aca6f098f5a428bda5355712341cef7c30c1b835ef444a9f5
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_035/text"
msgstr "“Look at my fingers. They've grown together. My hair has turned to noodles; it snaps when you touch it. And you ask when I can leave? I don't want to keep telling you off, but what have you ever done for this family?”"

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:37
#. source-sha256: 106aaba63ed85650982f748b18d1958d09549b15c99561591e1391f5648bf80a
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_036/text"
msgstr "...There's nothing left to say. Today's journey will remain my secret forever. Nobody wants to know. Nobody wants to listen. I get up and head for the door. My wife is still scolding me. If I'd known, I shouldn't have gone out today. I should have pretended I'd forgotten the alarm. Pretended I was sick too."

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:38
#. source-sha256: 14f147544962b9b93451dce1abe172b5712e5d3aa0ef9d6f05a01c19c6ba1ec8
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_037/text"
msgstr "A familiar pain stings my eyes. My vision blurs, everything overlaid with a sheet of rippled, wet glass. I avoid the crowded elevator and slip quietly down the stairs. All the while I keep wondering: what is this place? I don't mean this hospital. I mean this place where I live. What is it? How can I escape?"

#: res://timelines/08_wife_room.dtl:39
#. source-sha256: f2e229f6b5539c4da0944e49ca4f7e07c03df201a48d49ccace20d8b8846ddfa
msgid "Text/lj_08_wife_room_038/text"
msgstr "Lost in thought, I keep muttering, “What is this place?” A hand grabs my hair. The crooked-mouthed nurse pulls me close. Making sure no one is listening, she shields her mouth with one hand, leans into my ear, and tells me: this is a place where you die with nowhere to be buried."

#: res://timelines/09_ending.dtl:1
#. source-sha256: f323adac0b07465b9637d7da516014c57acf5315bda4d89f825b25181a8fa338
msgid "Text/lj_09_ending_000/text"
msgstr "[color=#696969][i]※Current location: Ending※[/i][/color]"

#: res://timelines/09_ending.dtl:3
#. source-sha256: b6bac85e9790bb8146350c8c5907f354edc7fe9a8d09bd55fe37f3716c77982e
msgid "Text/lj_09_ending_001/text"
msgstr "A place where you die with nowhere to be buried."

#: res://timelines/09_ending.dtl:5
#. source-sha256: 84592ae8aa1badcbbe582b3f128c77984de5eb070338fdddcf9b26628d3886b9
msgid "Text/lj_09_ending_002/text"
msgstr "The words fall into my ear like ash settling on water. I stand motionless. The crooked-mouthed nurse has already let go and slipped into the shadows of the corridor, as if she'd never been there."

#: res://timelines/09_ending.dtl:7
#. source-sha256: ae1448709256c55a09b0e7cd0aa66272438165391762cde3e78c848aa4eeb413
msgid "Text/lj_09_ending_003/text"
msgstr "One light in the stairwell has gone out. Another buzzes above my head. I steady myself against the wall and descend one step at a time. The scrape of my soles against concrete echoes through the empty building. There is no exit here, no one coming to take me home. My wife is still lying upstairs, her fingers grown together, her hair breaking at a touch. And downstairs, I finally admit that I can't leave this hospital either."

#: res://timelines/09_ending.dtl:9
#. source-sha256: 9a74a64a8d00651c631a809075ce498bf1eb3f1bbcb54a33bcb341bfa6e62671
msgid "Text/lj_09_ending_004/text"
msgstr "When I left home this morning, I was still counting the coins in my pocket, still fretting over those crumpled flowers. Now the flowers are gone and my shoes are torn. I can't even say how far I've traveled, or how many people I've seen who should never have been there. All I know is that from now on, no day will ever truly dawn."

#: res://timelines/09_ending.dtl:11
#. source-sha256: 21ef77aa6ac3c400e8d212870af0704c56291bc8fe5776f572e5b2c3db930e2d
msgid "Text/lj_09_ending_005/text"
msgstr "I push open the doors of the inpatient building. Outside lies the same gray road. It is neither dark nor light. I take one step, then a second, then a third. I keep walking until the door closes behind me with a dull thud."

#: res://timelines/09_ending.dtl:13
#. source-sha256: 3baed293f122bb7370b70b73d49565a7f6273d26501a72716c5cc6112d8771a6
msgid "Text/lj_09_ending_006/text"
msgstr "This is a place where you die with nowhere to be buried. And I have nowhere left to go, nowhere to escape."

#: res://timelines/10_morgue.dtl:1
#. source-sha256: 581710bdef2132a05dbcc60904512431c983e7fd25c54a6049b6292d11bc358a
msgid "Text/lj_10_morgue_000/text"
msgstr "[color=#696969][i]※Current location: Hospital — Morgue※[/i][/color]"

#: res://timelines/10_morgue.dtl:5
#. source-sha256: eb61cc9dd81d73b051ee91e34901fb10ac0510c5baf28824713de5ec695726bc
msgid "Text/lj_10_morgue_003/text"
msgstr "They say you can find good things in the morgue. I take a narrow path over to try my luck. If I do find something, my wife ought to be pleased."

#: res://timelines/10_morgue.dtl:7
#. source-sha256: 1250c93429a91a13dc4b62dc39794bc469f7062560fbeb575e300cca5d8bfcc0
msgid "Text/lj_10_morgue_004/text"
msgstr "I look around carefully. A few bodies still await burning on the floor, not laid out very neatly. Some relatives are howling nearby. Ah, life is decreed by heaven. When it's time to die, you die. The King of the Underworld doesn't care whether you cry. Your fate is set at birth, every detail written in his ledger. What good is crying?"

#: res://timelines/10_morgue.dtl:11
#. source-sha256: 3d87757ab491a2a9328d98152f79d120e65b1d7b4a673c8d99d2f21b7572e900
msgid "Text/lj_10_morgue_007/text"
msgstr "To the sound of their sobbing, I find several flower baskets in the morgue's trash bin. The flowers have all burned away, leaving empty baskets dusted with ashes. Luckily, one is fairly intact. I lift it and give it a shake. A pale yellow basket woven from earthworms, satisfyingly weighty in the hand and just the right size."

#: res://timelines/10_morgue.dtl:13
#. source-sha256: fa48fd0f47cb4aa248a3216efee1d0434acd5312d39ba3809ae97b122822e839
msgid "Text/lj_10_morgue_008/text"
msgstr "I can use it to carry flowers."

#: res://timelines/10_morgue.dtl:21
#. source-sha256: d6da48a33e298ad52938b42ce73b439c2d6bc9b8800e07682bcc48a287265cc7
msgid "Text/lj_10_morgue_019/text"
msgstr "Back at the morgue. The people who were crying are leaving now, supporting one another, wiping their tears with red cloths. They mutter words only they can hear. The weather is still dreadful, as though snow is coming. The clouds have turned very white, the sky grayer by the moment."

#: res://timelines/10_morgue.dtl:26
#. source-sha256: 5ed24a404ada297e8aa8baa9849df6b23c8b70baf960907f131aaaa942d1b737
msgid "Text/lj_10_morgue_025/text"
msgstr "No one is left here. I take off my glasses, breathe on the lenses, and wipe them a little cleaner."

